me to start calling on these companies  more aggressively to make sure they paid  their bills you want to maintain a good  relationship with your clients but  you're also running a business not a  charity and bills need to get paid for  future clients you may also want to run  a credit check on them before you extend  any  kind of terms to them number four give  an incentive to pay early some clients  might have a policy of only paying after  60 90 or even 120 days the bigger the  client is generally the more you have to  wait to get paid one way to flip this  around is to offer an incentive to pay  early depending on what your margins are  and how badly you need the money you can  give a discount say two to five percent  of the invoice if they pay right away  instead of waiting some customers will  take you up on it because it also helps  them and it puts money into your pocket  immediately number five make sure you  invoice on time a lot of entrepreneurs  are so busy running their businesses and  trying to get new customers but they put  off administrative tasks like invoicing  the longer you wait to invoice the  longer you wait to get paid as soon as  you're able to annoys your clients you  can get the money as quickly as possible  number six change your billing structure  try as much as possible to get the money  up front and deliver the products or  services afterwards for example when I  work with clients I use a retainer  system they hire me for project which  may include work for up to six months or  a year I'll build them up front for the  entire project and then deliver  according to the schedule we set up if  you're selling a product think about  offering some kind of subscription model  where they pay in advance for a year and  they get a certain quantity every month  you can consider offering a slight  discount in exchange for them making a  long-term commitment to you and for  paying upfront  number seven accept credit cards share  their credit card fees they have to pay  but there are also some major advantages  to accepting credit cards as a payment  option the first is that you get the  money quickly either instantly or by the  end of the day customers are also more  likely to spend more money when they pay  by credit card compared the one they pay  by cash you might be saving a little bit  by not using credit cards but you're  also probably leaving a lot of money on  the table  number eight factor your receivables if  you have significant money owed to you  it's possible to sell the receivables to  a factoring company they'll give you a  percentage of the total amount and  return for you getting immediate cash  typically the larger your clients are  the greater percentage you'll get  because it's less risks for them to take  on factoring generally is still  expensive and only recommend using it as  a last resort  number nine sell excess inventory if you  have inventory that is just taking up  space try to sell a lot for a quick cash  injection you may not turn a large  profit on it but if it's not being used  then the best value you may get from it  is to trade it for media cash note that  I wouldn't recommend doing this for  inventory that you're going to use in  your business selling inventory that you  will eventually need as steeply  discounted price will have a long-term  negative impact on your business  number 10 negotiate terms with your  suppliers this in theory is a good idea  and the textbooks will tell you to do it  the idea here is to look at everyone who  you owe money to so your suppliers and  try to delay your payment to them for as  long as possible it makes sense because  if you're delaying when money goes out  you're improving your short-term cash  flow here's what I don't like the  strategy  it can sour your relationship with your  supplier you want to count on your  suppliers for quality products and  services if you're in a bind they need  something quickly you want to know that  your suppliers have your back you think  they're gonna give you their very best  and bend over backwards for you if  you're stretching them out on when you  pay them think about it if they're a  small business owner then they likely  have cashflow concerns as well and are  looking at their accounts receivable ie  you for some relief if it's a big  company then get the best terms that you  can but it's a small company I'd be very  hesitant in negotiating terms in my  business I pay my suppliers as soon as  the invoice me I pay ahead of when  they're expecting with no discount  because I want the best from them and I  get it  number eleven create a referral program  another great way to boost cash flow  through sales is to ask for referrals  from your existing clients again they  like you know you trust you enjoy  working with you maybe they know someone  else who could also benefit from what  you do you could create an elaborate  program with incentives or just call up  your best customers to take about the  lunch to ask for their help in thinking  of other people who might be a client  for you really depends on the customer  some love the recognition and others  just do it because you ask them to  either way getting new clients in the  door is a great way to improve both the  short term and long term cash flow of  your business and referrals on one of  the best ways to get ideal clients  onboard number twelve refinance short  term into long term debt the people you  owe money to they want to get paid back  and for that to happen you still have to  be in business talk to your lenders and  see if is a way to negotiate a better  deal in particular you're looking for  ways to move the short term debt which  is money that's owed within the next  year and convert it into long-term debt  money that's owed beyond one year this  will give you some cash flow relief that  you can hopefully use to continue  growing your business number thirteen  sell and leaseback  another creative way to improve your  cash flow is to look at your fixed  assets and see if there's anything you  can sell and then lease back to the  business this works particularly well  with expensive assets like land and  buildings the idea is to sell your asset  to a company which gives you immediate  money but then you create a lease  agreement where you pay an ongoing fee  for the right to use the asset it will  increase your regular payments out but  gives you a monetary injection that you  can help use to solve an immediate cash  crunch no you can only do this once  number fourteen convert debt to equity  this is an even more creative option and  one you should really only use if you  have a good relationship with the people  you owe money to the idea here is to  take the people you need to pay and swap  the amount you owe them for equity in  your business you give them a piece of  your company and they erase the debt you  have to figure out how much you think  your company is worth as well as how  much you're going to give up to them  more importantly you'll want to really  ask yourself if you want this person to  be a part of your business long term or  not because the last thing you need is a  minority shareholder who adds no value  and causes problems for the company it's  not my favorite option but it's an  option so I wanted to share it with you  number fifteen bootstrap this is my top  suggestion of all I hate spending money  until I'm making money anybody can spend  money but it takes a lot of effort to  learn how to make it if you have a goal  to accomplish something and you think  you need X amount of dollars to do it  find a way to start smaller and without  spending any money prove to yourself  that you can make a little bit of money  just by putting in your time then when  you know how to make money you can spend  money to expend it's good money to  invest because you know it's gonna work  you're just expanding on what you've  already shown is effective it's hard  work it takes a lot more time but will  help ensure that you're building your  business the right way  don't spend until you earn thank you for  joining me for another edition of ask  Evan I hope you liked the video if you  did and you want to see more please give  it a thumbs up below it makes me want to  do more of these for you and I'd love to  hear you have to think if you have a  question about this video or you have a  question about your own business I'd  love to hear it if you want to leave it  in the comment section below so thank  you and we'll see you on the next  episode  you
 

